### External FTP Pull Ingestion (v3.3) — Component 1: The Gatekeeper Technical Details

#### Architecture & Data Flow

```
Client (React)
    │  POST /v1/ingest/ftp/connect (host, port, username, password, allow_insecure, duration...)
    ▼
FastAPI Router (ftp_routes.py)
    │  _resolve_current_user() → User
    ▼
FTP Service (ext_ftp_service.py)
    ├──► 1. _check_rate_limit(user_id)
    │       Redis INCR ext_ftp:rate:{user_id} (Window=300s, Max=5)
    │       Raises 429 FtpRateLimitError if exceeded
    │
    ├──► 2. _probe_ftp_connection(host, port, username, password, allow_insecure)
    │       ftplib.FTP_TLS probe → auth() → prot_p() → login()
    │       If TLS fails & allow_insecure=True → fallback ftplib.FTP
    │       Raises 400 FtpTlsRejectedError, 401 FtpAuthError, 504 FtpConnectionError
    │
    ├──► 3. Fernet Credential Encryption (fernet_vault.py)
    │       fernet_encrypt(password) → FERNET_KEY (32-byte url-safe base64)
    │
    └──► 4. Redis Credential Vault Storage
            SET ext_ftp:creds:{user_id} payload JSON (ex=1800s idle TTL)
            Returns FtpConnectResponse (host, username, protocol, state, idle_ttl, expiry)
```

#### Stateful Disconnect Flows

```
POST /v1/ingest/ftp/disconnect?force=false (Normal Disconnect / Graceful Draining)
    │
    ├──► Active FTP jobs == 0  ──► Wipe Redis ext_ftp:creds:{user_id} ──► 200 OK
    └──► Active FTP jobs > 0   ──► Set state="draining" in Redis     ──► 409 Conflict (FtpSessionDrainingError)

POST /v1/ingest/ftp/disconnect?force=true (Force Nuke)
    │
    ├──► Cancel all pending/in_progress AsyncIngestionJob (provider="external_ftp")
    ├──► If delete_completed_files=true:
    │       Delete DatasetFolderFilesMapping rows for user
    │       Check SELECT COUNT(*) on DatasetFolderFilesMapping for each file_id
    │       If ref_count == 0 ──► os.remove(physical_path) + delete UploadedFile row
    └──► Wipe Redis ext_ftp:creds:{user_id} ──► 200 OK
```

